    "description": "The Impulsivity Scale for Children (ISC) is an 8-item self-report measure assessing impulsive tendencies in children, covering difficulties with inhibitory control and acting without forethought. It is used to screen for impulsivity-related concerns in developmental and clinical research settings.",
